The End is a firearm the [[Divinity/The Narrative/Menhir|Menhir]] gave the Party when they called on it. It is shaped like a revolver, of a white material like ivory filigreed with gold that shimmers when the light moves, and it leaves a faint afterimage as it travels. Nothing about it reads as magic; those who examine it find no harmonies to take apart, only a question mark where a purpose would be. Its chamber takes gold spikes about the length of a finger, seventeen of which came with it in a plain card box. [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] found no magic in the spikes either.

The Party call it the godkiller. A single spike fired from it into one standing stone brought down the whole ring of the Menhir and killed it.

A [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] liaison officer, shown the spikes and asked whether the Party had one, named the same thing: a spike of a rare gold metal, the only way her people know of to kill a [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]].
